(If I may critique an earlier part of your game)

Personally, I think if you're playing a combat wombat, you shouldn't use any
gain level items. The monsters you have to kill to gain experience and level
will help you exercise stats, find treasure, and build weapons skills. This
goes double for after you reach level 14 -- you don't need to be level 30 to
ascend as a wombat. (Spellcasting classes are a different story, perhaps.)
The lower your levels, the easier the monsters will be, and you  likely
won't be any better at killing things at level 30 than you would be at level
14. (My wombats usually end up being level 15 or 16 by the time I ascend
them, but only due to killing things as I descend and ascend the dungeon.)

Also, #twoweaponing helps -- train a primary weapon artifact and a good
secondary weapon (like a silver sabre) up as high as you can get, and then
switch to #twoweapon for the duration of the game.

